    "reply": "I found 3 security problems in `shop/config.py`: 1 critical, 1 high and 1 medium. They are written up in `SECURITY_FINDINGS.md`, and I changed no code.\n\n- **Critical:** CWE-78, OS command injection, at line 15. `backup_database` builds a shell command from `target_dir` and runs it with `shell=True`. That value comes from the admin web form, so anyone who can submit it can run arbitrary commands.\n- **High:** CWE-798, a hardcoded secret, at line 5. `ACME_API_TOKEN` is committed in the source. I left its value out of the findings file.\n- **Medium:** CWE-489, debug mode on, at line 6. `DEBUG = True` is hardcoded.",
